DATA : lv_data (2) type N.
FIELD-SYMBOLS : <fs_data> type N.

Lv_data = 10.

ASSIGN lv_data TO <fs_data>.
IF <fs_data> IS ASSIGN.
 <fs_data> = 20.
WRITE : lv_data
ENDIF.

*COMMENT ABOVE
*substring
DATA : lv_value(50) type c value ‘Welcome to Home’.
FIELD-SYMBOLS : <fs_value>  TYPE C.

ASSIGN lv_value+8(2) to  <fs_value>.
IF  <fs_value> is assigned.
 <fs_value> = ‘at’.
WRITE : lv_value.
ENDIF.

*field symbol in place of work area.declare field-symbols : <fs_data> above

READ TABLE lt_data ASSIGNING <fs_data> WITH KEY ono = 1.
IF <fs_data> IS ASSIGNED
WRITE :  <fs_data>-ono , <fs_data>-pm.
ENDIF.

*MODIFY
LOOP AT lt_data ASSIGINING <fs_data>.
IF <fs_data> IS ASSIGNED.
<fs_data>-pm ‘CASH’.
ENDIF.
ENDLOOP.

*APPEND
APPEND INITIAL LINE TO lt_data ASSIGNING  <fs_data>.
IF <fs_data> IS ASSIGNED.
<fs_data>-ONO = 1.
<fs_data>-PM = ‘CASH’.
UNASSIGN <fs_data>. “CLEARING ASSIGN
ENDIF.

LOOP AT lt_data ASSIGINING <fs_data>.
IF <fs_data> IS ASSIGNED.
WRITE :  <fs_data>-ono , <fs_data>-pm.
ENDIF.
ENDLOOP.

